WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.176
This session follows Seven E sections five and six. The central question is what changed for this person and what that change means now.
本节依7E第五及第六节，核心是这个人改变了什么，以及现在意味着什么。

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:20.808
Older age can alter reserve and presentation, but it does not make every patient frail, confused, dependent or incapable of deciding about care.
高龄可改变储备表现，却不使每个人都虚弱、混乱、依赖或不能决定照护。

00:00:20.808 --> 00:00:31.728
We will connect physiology and medicines to observations, then make communication and movement safer. A category name should improve care rather than replace assessment.
我们把生理及药物连到观察，再使沟通移动更安全；类别名称应改善照护，而非替代评估。

00:00:31.728 --> 00:00:40.032
An original evolving case will test the reasoning. It is not a school assessment answer or a claim that reading certifies a handling skill.
原创展开病例将检验推理，不是学校考核答案，也不表示读完就认证搬运技能。

00:00:40.032 --> 00:00:51.984
Ask the patient what they normally do and what feels different today. Useful function includes walking to the kitchen, preparing food, managing medicines or following a conversation.
应先问本人平常做什么、今天哪里不同。有用功能可包括走到厨房、备餐、管药及跟随交谈。

00:00:51.984 --> 00:01:03.216
Ask a reliable witness when the last usual interaction occurred. A vague statement that the patient is often confused does not explain a new loss of attention or mobility.
需问可靠目击者末次正常互动何时。含糊说患者常混乱，不能解释新注意或活动丧失。

00:01:03.216 --> 00:01:14.208
Distinguish chronic limitations from acute changes without dismissing either. A person with dementia can develop delirium, stroke, injury or infection.
要区分慢性限制与急性改变，却不能轻视任何一方。痴呆者也可有谵妄、卒中、损伤或感染。

00:01:14.208 --> 00:01:24.888
Record who supplied the baseline and what remains uncertain. A later handover is safer when the next team can judge the reliability of the comparison.
应记基线来源及未知，让下队可判断比较可靠性，交接才更安全。

00:01:24.888 --> 00:01:36.120
Physiological reserve is the ability to respond to additional demand. Someone can meet daily needs and then deteriorate when illness, dehydration or injury adds stress.
生理储备是应对额外需求的能力。有人日常足够，却在病、脱水或伤增压时恶化。

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:44.496
Age-related changes and chronic disease may reduce that margin, but the amount varies substantially between people and organ systems.
年龄相关变化及慢病可减少余量，但不同人及器官差异很大。

00:01:44.496 --> 00:01:54.168
Do not learn a universal linear rate of aging or assume every organ fails to the same degree. Establish the actual function and current signs.
不能背统一线性老化速度，也不能认每器官同程度衰竭；需确定真实功能及当前征象。

00:01:54.168 --> 00:02:05.616
The practical implication is a low threshold to investigate meaningful new change, not permission to call all abnormalities normal aging or to treat every older person identically.
实践上应对有意义新变化积极评估，不是把异常都叫正常老化，也不是人人同治。

00:02:05.616 --> 00:02:16.872
Vascular stiffness and changes in cardiac filling or conduction can influence the response to illness. Chronic disease and medicines may contribute as much as age itself.
血管硬度、心充盈或传导变化可影响病中反应，慢病和药物贡献可能不亚于年龄。

00:02:16.872 --> 00:02:25.944
A normal-range pulse does not exclude blood loss or infection, especially with a rate-limiting medicine. Assess the whole perfusion picture.
尤其服限率药时，脉在正常范围不能排失血或感染，需评整体灌注。

00:02:25.944 --> 00:02:39.696
Compare pressure with a reliable baseline and current symptoms. A relative fall may be concerning, but one systolic value below one hundred twenty does not automatically prove hypovolemia or require fluid.
应把血压与可靠基线及当前症状比。相对下降可令人担忧，但一次收缩压低于120不自动证明低容量或需补液。

00:02:39.696 --> 00:02:51.960
Likewise, hypertension is not harmless because it is common in older adults. New neurological, chest or breathing findings still require assessment through the appropriate pathway.
同样，高血压常见不表示无害；新神经、胸或呼吸发现仍需按适当路径评估。

00:02:51.960 --> 00:03:01.296
Chest-wall changes, muscle weakness and chronic lung disease may reduce breathing reserve. Cough and clearance can also be impaired.
胸壁变化、肌弱及慢肺病可减少呼吸储备，咳嗽清除也可受损。

00:03:01.296 --> 00:03:12.432
New tachypnea may be important even without fever or a dramatic complaint. Assess depth, effort, air movement and mental response as well as saturation.
无热或明显主诉时，新快呼吸也可重要；需评深度、努力、气流和精神反应，也看血氧。

00:03:12.432 --> 00:03:24.552
Do not apply a textbook age formula as proof that a low oxygen value is acceptable. Use the actual clinical oxygen pathway and identify any established chronic target.
不能用教材年龄公式证明低氧值可接受；应依真实给氧路径，并识别既定慢病目标。

00:03:24.552 --> 00:03:36.384
A first crackle or chronic edema does not alone establish heart failure, but neither should new findings be dismissed. Use history, distribution, trend and the full assessment.
第一次听到啰音或慢水肿不能单证心衰，但新发现也不能被忽略；需结合史、分布、趋势及全评估。

00:03:36.384 --> 00:03:46.776
Some people need longer to hear, process or answer a question. Provide support and time before deciding that the response represents cognitive failure.
有些人需更久听取、处理或回答。认其认知失败前，应先支持并给时间。

00:03:46.776 --> 00:03:58.752
Acute confusion, new focal weakness or a major functional decline is not explained by getting older. Check breathing, glucose, perfusion and relevant neurological findings.
急混乱、新局灶弱或明显功能下降，不由年老本身解释；需查呼吸、糖、灌注及相关神经。

00:03:58.752 --> 00:04:12.072
After a fall, head injury may be subtle or have delayed symptoms, especially with anticoagulant use. Absence of severe headache or a remembered head strike cannot independently clear it.
跌倒后头伤可隐匿或延迟，尤其用抗凝时；没有剧头痛或不记得撞头，不能单独排除。

00:04:12.072 --> 00:04:22.800
Age-associated anatomy may help explain risk but does not guarantee a particular bleed or outcome. Preserve alternatives while prioritizing urgent assessment.
年龄解剖可解释风险，却不保证某种出血或结果；要保鉴别并优先急评。

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:35.640
Kidney and liver function influence drug handling, and acute illness may change clearance. Do not assume every older adult has identical impairment or that an old normal result proves current safety.
肾肝功能影响药物处理，急病可改清除；不能认每高龄者同样受损，也不能靠旧正常结果证明现在安全。

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:47.952
Reduced intake, vomiting, diarrhea or diuretic effects can reduce circulating volume. Heart and kidney disease may simultaneously increase the risk of fluid overload.
少摄入、吐泻或利尿效应可减循环容量，心肾病又可同时增过负荷风险。

00:04:47.952 --> 00:04:59.784
Use perfusion, breathing, urine history and response to guide the real care plan. Dry mouth or skin tenting alone is insufficient to diagnose dehydration in older skin.
应依灌注、呼吸、尿史及反应指导真实计划；老化皮肤中，单口干或皮帐不足以诊脱水。

00:04:59.784 --> 00:05:09.744
This is not an automatic fluid, potassium or dose-adjustment instruction. Use the permitted pathway and clinical consultation for the actual patient.
这不是自动补液、补钾或改药量指令；需依真实患者获准路径及临床咨询。

00:05:09.744 --> 00:05:22.416
Skin may be more vulnerable to shear or adhesive injury, and some people have fragile bones or painful joints. Ask about previous handling difficulties and look at the actual tissue.
皮肤可更易剪切或胶伤，有些人骨脆关节痛；应问既往搬运困难并看真实组织。

00:05:22.416 --> 00:05:32.496
Use appropriate padding and aids, and remove necessary adhesive gently. Do not drag a patient across a surface or use their arms as lifting handles.
应适当垫护及用辅助器械，需除胶时要轻；不能拖擦患者或把手臂当提把。

00:05:32.496 --> 00:05:42.336
Expose only what is needed for an adequate assessment and cover again. Warmth and privacy are active parts of care, not optional finishing touches.
要足够而不过度暴露，评完再盖；保暖隐私是主动照护，不是可有可无的收尾。

00:05:42.336 --> 00:05:52.344
Reassess after the move for pain, skin injury, breathing and device position. A technically completed transfer is not proof that it was harmless.
搬后需复痛、皮肤伤、呼吸及器械位置；转移完成不证明没有伤害。

00:05:52.344 --> 00:06:02.928
An acute coronary event may occur without classic chest pain. New unexplained weakness, dyspnea, syncope or nausea can be part of the presentation.
急性冠脉事件可没有典型胸痛，新不明无力、气促、晕厥或恶心可参与表现。

00:06:02.928 --> 00:06:14.136
Ask what happened today that prompted help and how activity differs from usual. Do not assume the patient would necessarily describe a dangerous symptom using textbook words.
应问今天何事使其求助，以及活动和平时有何不同；不能假定危险症状一定用教材词描述。

00:06:14.136 --> 00:06:25.392
Perform appropriate assessment, including an ECG when indicated, without delaying primary care. The absence of pain does not remove the need for the cardiac differential.
有指征时应做包括ECG的适当评估，但不延主要照护；无痛不取消心脏鉴别。

00:06:25.392 --> 00:06:36.024
Other causes of weakness remain possible. Atypical presentation should widen useful assessment rather than force every older person into an infarction diagnosis.
无力仍可有其他原因。非典型概念应扩有用评估，而不是把每位高龄者强诊心梗。

00:06:36.024 --> 00:06:49.200
Infection can present with a muted temperature response or new functional loss. Consider it when an older person becomes acutely unwell, but do not let it hide stroke, injury or medicine effects.
感染可温度反应不明显或出现新功能丧失。高龄者急病需考虑，但不能因此遮卒中、伤或药物效应。

00:06:49.200 --> 00:07:02.064
Assess new respiratory symptoms, wounds, urinary-localizing symptoms and other relevant sources. A source search should be focused and respectful rather than indiscriminate exposure.
要评新呼吸症、伤口、泌尿定位症及其他相关源；查源需重点尊重，不是不分情况暴露。

00:07:02.064 --> 00:07:13.008
Bacteriuria or odor alone does not prove a symptomatic urinary infection. Delirium without local urinary or systemic signs needs a broader cause assessment.
单独菌尿或异味不证明有症状尿路感染。无泌尿定位或全身征的谵妄，需要更广原因评估。

00:07:13.008 --> 00:07:25.560
Do not wait for hypotension, high fever or a positive laboratory test to recognize credible deterioration. Use the actual local sepsis pathway and ongoing clinical picture.
可信恶化不能等低压、高热或阳性化验才识别；应依真实本地脓毒路径及持续临床图景。

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:37.248
Polypharmacy means multiple concurrent medicines. The count alone does not prove inappropriate treatment, but it increases the need for accurate history and interaction awareness.
多重用药指同时使用多种药，数量本身不证明不恰当，却增加准确药史及相互作用关注的需要。

00:07:37.248 --> 00:07:48.048
Medicines can cause symptoms, worsen another illness or hide a usual response. Consider all three rather than naming an adverse effect and stopping assessment.
药可致症、加重另一病或掩常见反应。应三者都考虑，不能点出不良反应就结束评估。

00:07:48.048 --> 00:07:59.232
Ask about new prescriptions, dose changes, missed or repeated doses and nonprescription products. A blister pack does not prove which dose was actually taken.
要问新方、改量、漏服重服及非处方品；泡罩包不能证明哪量已实际服下。

00:07:59.232 --> 00:08:10.776
Report the evidence and seek the appropriate plan. This lecture does not authorize stopping chronic treatment, reversing an anticoagulant or changing another clinician's regimen.
应报告证据并取得适当计划；本课不授权停慢药、逆转抗凝或改他人方案。

00:08:10.776 --> 00:08:20.616
Beta blockers and some other medicines can limit heart-rate responses. A pulse of seventy is not automatically reassuring in an unwell patient taking one.
β阻滞剂及某些药可限制心率反应。服药病人脉七十不自动令人放心。

00:08:20.616 --> 00:08:30.864
Look at responsiveness, skin, pulse quality, breathing and pressure relative to baseline. Ask about the actual last dose, not only the medicine name.
需看反应、皮肤、脉质、呼吸及相对基线血压，并问真实末次量，不只药名。

00:08:30.864 --> 00:08:40.176
A medicine can contribute to a slow pulse or low pressure, but a concurrent bleed, infection or cardiac problem may also be present.
药可促慢脉低压，同时也可有出血、感染或心病。

00:08:40.176 --> 00:08:49.176
Avoid the shortcut that one mechanism explains everything. Use the relevant clinical pathway and reassess after permitted care.
不能用一种机制解释一切的捷径，需依相关路径并在获准照护后复评。

00:08:49.176 --> 00:09:00.384
Ask specifically about anticoagulants and antiplatelet medicines rather than relying only on the phrase blood thinner. Different agents have different effects and reversal plans.
应具体问抗凝及抗血小板药，不能只靠稀血药一词；不同药效及逆转计划不同。

00:09:00.384 --> 00:09:11.280
After a fall, seek direct observations of head contact, loss of consciousness and subsequent change. A patient may not recall the mechanism accurately.
跌倒后需找撞头、失去意识及随后变化的直接观察；患者未必能准确记机制。

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:22.368
A small visible bruise does not measure the extent of internal injury. Delayed confusion or reduced function requires assessment even when the initial injury seemed minor.
小瘀斑不能量内部伤。即使最初看似小伤，延迟混乱或功能减也需评估。

00:09:22.368 --> 00:09:33.600
Do not give an unverified reversal treatment or force the patient to walk to prove stability. Communicate the exact agent history and uncertainty to the receiving team.
不能给未核逆转治疗，也不能逼走来证明稳定；需向接收队报准确药史及未知。

00:09:33.600 --> 00:09:45.144
Opioids, benzodiazepines and some antipsychotic or other medicines can affect alertness and balance. Combinations and acute changes in clearance may increase risk.
阿片、苯二氮䓬及部分抗精神等药可影响清醒和平衡，组合及清除急变可增风险。

00:09:45.144 --> 00:09:53.928
Assess breathing effectiveness as well as saturation and rate. A sleepy patient on oxygen may still be ventilating inadequately.
需评呼吸效能，也看血氧次数；吸氧嗜睡者仍可通气不足。

00:09:53.928 --> 00:10:06.048
Clarify what was actually taken and when. Preserve possible trauma, infection, glucose or neurological causes rather than concluding from the medicine list alone.
需澄实际服什么何时，并保伤、感染、糖或神经原因，不能只凭药单结论。

00:10:06.048 --> 00:10:16.248
Support the observed threat through the correct pathway. Medication awareness is not permission for an empirical reversal drug or independent chronic dose change.
需经正确路径支持已见威胁。懂药不授权经验性逆转剂或自行改长期量。

00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:29.496
Diuretics can change volume and electrolytes, but not every class lowers potassium. Combine the medicine history with actual losses, breathing, perfusion and available measurements.
利尿可改容量电解质，却非每类降钾；需把药史与实际丢失、呼吸、灌注及可得测量结合。

00:10:29.496 --> 00:10:40.296
Some diabetes medicines create recurrent low-glucose risk. A single corrected value or meal is not sufficient to dismiss the underlying medication problem.
某些糖尿病药可使低糖复发，一次纠值或一餐不足以忽略根本药物问题。

00:10:40.296 --> 00:10:54.264
Anticholinergic effects may contribute retention, constipation, dry mouth or confusion. Do not automatically label urinary symptoms infection or use dry mouth alone as a fluid-bolus indication.
抗胆碱效应可促潴留、便秘、口干或混乱；不能把尿症自动叫感染，也不能仅口干就推液。

00:10:54.264 --> 00:11:04.608
Seek a coherent timeline of changes rather than collecting a list without interpretation. Several mechanisms can coexist and require a supported plan.
要取得连贯变化时间线，不是只收药名而不解释；多机制可并存，需要支持下计划。

00:11:04.608 --> 00:11:14.592
Ask about prescriptions, over-the-counter medicines, supplements and products from another person. Explain why the information matters without blaming the patient.
需问处方、非处方、补充品及借用产品，并解释意义，不责备。

00:11:14.592 --> 00:11:24.168
Verify the exact product and actual last intake when possible. A dispensing label describes the intended plan, not proof of adherence.
可行时核准确产品及实际末次服；配药标签描述预定方案，不证明依从。

00:11:24.168 --> 00:11:35.760
Ask about cost, side effects, access, swallowing and assistance when relevant. Missed treatment can reflect a practical barrier rather than deliberate refusal.
相关时应问费用、副作用、获得、吞咽及协助。漏治可反映实际障碍，不一定故意拒绝。

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:47.712
Obtain permission before collecting relevant packaging or contacting collateral. Do not search unrelated personal storage simply because a textbook suggests gathering all medicines.
收相关包装或联络旁证前应取得同意，不能因教材建议收所有药，就搜无关私人储物。

00:11:47.712 --> 00:12:00.096
Nancy uses the GEMS framework to organize geriatric, environmental, medical and social considerations. It complements rather than replaces immediate assessment of life threats.
Nancy用GEMS组织高龄、环境、医疗及社会考虑，补充但不替即时生命威胁评估。

00:12:00.096 --> 00:12:11.064
Environmental observations can reveal cold exposure, access barriers or a fall mechanism. Describe what you see without assuming that a cluttered home proves neglect.
环境可显冷暴露、通行障碍或跌倒机制；需描述所见，不能认家乱就证明忽视。

00:12:11.064 --> 00:12:22.968
Medical context includes the current complaint, baseline and medicines. Social context includes support for meals, mobility or treatment and what the patient wishes to preserve.
医疗背景含当前主诉、基线及药；社会背景含进餐、活动或治疗支持，以及本人想保留什么。

00:12:22.968 --> 00:12:31.896
Use the information for a safe plan and appropriate referral. Do not delay urgent conveyance to complete a detailed social inventory.
信息应用于安全计划及适当转介，不能为详细社会清单延紧急转运。

00:12:31.896 --> 00:12:41.472
Address the patient respectfully by the name they prefer. Avoid infantilizing terms or speaking only to family while the patient is present.
应尊重地用本人偏好称呼，避免幼儿化称谓，也不要当面只对家属说。

00:12:41.472 --> 00:12:51.264
Check that hearing aids and glasses are available and working when needed, and reduce competing noise. Shouting may distort the message instead of helping.
需要时应确认助听器眼镜可用有效，并减背景噪声；喊叫可能使信息失真。

00:12:51.264 --> 00:13:02.424
Use short clear questions, allow time and obtain an interpreter or other support when appropriate. A slow answer is not itself evidence of incapacity.
应短清楚问、留时间，并按需口译或支持；回答慢本身不证明无能力。

00:13:02.424 --> 00:13:11.712
Check understanding by asking for an explanation in the patient's own words. Do not confuse repeating a phrase with understanding the particular decision.
要请本人用自己的话解释以核理解；不能把重复一句话等同理解具体决定。

00:13:11.712 --> 00:13:22.488
Older age, dementia, hearing loss or a care-home address does not independently determine capacity. Assess the actual decision using supported communication.
高龄、痴呆、听损或住护理院，不独立决定能力；需用支持沟通评具体决定。

00:13:22.488 --> 00:13:33.096
An acute change may interfere with understanding or communication, but it still requires evidence and the actual consent framework rather than an age-based shortcut.
急变可影响理解沟通，但仍需证据及真实同意框架，不能走年龄捷径。

00:13:33.096 --> 00:13:43.752
A family member is not automatically entitled to override a capable adult. Identify the appropriate decision-maker and authority when a substitute is needed.
家属不自动可推翻有能力成人；需替代时应核正确决定者及权限。

00:13:43.752 --> 00:13:56.232
Use clinical consultation and the established urgent-care process when uncertainty affects safety. Record the explanation, responses and reasoning rather than merely writing confused.
未知影响安全时需临床咨询及既定紧急程序，并记解释、回应和推理，不只写混乱。

00:13:56.232 --> 00:14:06.744
Delirium commonly involves an acute or fluctuating change in attention and awareness. The onset and course matter more than whether the patient is agitated.
谵妄常涉及急性或波动的注意觉醒改变；起始过程比是否躁动更重要。

00:14:06.744 --> 00:14:15.480
A chronic dementia history gives a baseline to compare, not a reason to dismiss new change. Both processes can occur together.
慢痴呆史提供比较基线，不是忽略新变化的理由，两过程可同时发生。

00:14:15.480 --> 00:14:28.896
Consider breathing, glucose, perfusion, infection, neurological disease, pain, retention and medicine effects according to the presentation. Do not stop after one plausible explanation.
应依表现考虑呼吸、糖、灌注、感染、神经病、痛、潴留及药效，不能见一个合理解释就停。

00:14:28.896 --> 00:14:41.616
Treat urgent threats and investigate through the appropriate pathway. Reversibility and recovery are variable; recognizing delirium does not promise an immediate complete return to baseline.
应处理急威胁并经适当路径查因。可逆性及恢复有差异，认谵妄不保证立刻完全回基线。

00:14:41.616 --> 00:14:52.344
A patient may become unusually quiet rather than restless. New withdrawal, poor attention or reduced movement can still signal serious illness.
患者可异常安静而非躁动；新退缩、注意差或活动减仍可提示重病。

00:14:52.344 --> 00:15:03.288
Ask for the usual routine and directly observe current responses. A caregiver's description of a quiet personality is not a substitute for the patient's actual attention today.
需问平日规律并直接看当前回应。家属说性格安静，不能替今天真实注意评估。

00:15:03.288 --> 00:15:13.224
Repeat breathing, glucose, perfusion and relevant neurological findings. Sedation, exhaustion and other medical causes remain possible.
要复呼吸、糖、灌注及相关神经发现，镇静、耗竭及其他医疗原因仍可能。

00:15:13.224 --> 00:15:23.184
Use calm orientation and support, but do not mistake reduced activity after an intervention for improvement without checking function and physiology.
可平静定向支持，但干预后活动减，不能在未核功能生理时误当改善。

00:15:23.184 --> 00:15:33.048
Ask what preceded the fall, whether it was witnessed and how long the patient remained down. Separate a reported trip from an unexplained collapse.
要问跌前发生什么、是否目击及倒地多久，并分转述绊倒与不明倒下。

00:15:33.048 --> 00:15:44.280
Assess both the cause and the resulting injury. Infection, bleeding, glucose disturbance or a rhythm problem can coexist with a fracture or head injury.
需同时评原因及结果，感染、出血、糖扰或节律问题可与骨折头伤并存。

00:15:44.280 --> 00:15:54.336
A new loss of mobility is important even with mild pain. Do not use absence of deformity or a patient's wish to avoid inconvenience to exclude injury.
即使痛轻，新活动丧失也重要。不能凭无畸形或患者不想麻烦就排伤。

00:15:54.336 --> 00:16:04.656
Choose a safe movement plan and appropriate spinal or limb protection. Do not force standing or orthostatic testing in an unstable or injured patient.
需选安全移动及适当脊肢保护，不能强迫不稳定或受伤者站立、做体位试验。

00:16:04.656 --> 00:16:13.176
A patient saying they can walk is useful but not sufficient. Current clinical risk and observed ability must support the plan.
本人说能走有用，却不足够；当前临床风险及所见能力都需支持计划。

00:16:13.176 --> 00:16:24.624
Use the actual movement assessment before staged mobility. A serious cardiac, respiratory or limb threat may require a nonambulatory method rather than a trial walk.
分段活动前需真实移动评估；严重心、呼吸或肢体威胁可需非步行方式，而不是试走。

00:16:24.624 --> 00:16:35.808
If more than minimal assistance would be needed or symptoms worsen, stop and change the plan. Additional manual lifters are not automatically safer than a suitable aid.
若需超过轻微协助或症恶化，应停并改计划；多加人工不自动比适当辅助安全。

00:16:35.808 --> 00:16:47.856
Communicate the plan, protect attachments and reassess after each meaningful stage. Do not turn a school practice sequence into a mandatory mobility challenge for every patient.
需沟通、保护附件并在有意义阶段后复评；学校练习序列不能变成人人必做活动挑战。

00:16:47.856 --> 00:16:58.200
Some patients cannot safely or comfortably lie flat because of spinal curvature, pain or breathing difficulty. Forcing them flat may worsen the problem.
部分患者因脊柱弯曲、痛或呼吸难，无法安全舒适平卧；强压平可加重。

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:06.216
Support the natural position and fill relevant gaps with suitable padding, while maintaining the actual injury and airway plan.
应支持自然体位，以合适垫填相关空隙，同时维真实损伤及气道计划。

00:17:06.216 --> 00:17:15.456
Padding is not a reason to ignore new neurological symptoms or to build an unstable stack. Check secure support and equipment fit.
垫护不能成为忽略新神经症或堆不稳垫的理由；需核稳定支撑及器械适配。

00:17:15.456 --> 00:17:25.104
Reassess breathing, pain, perfusion and neurological findings after positioning or movement. Ask the patient whether the new position helps.
摆位移动后需复呼吸、痛、灌注及神经，并问新位置是否有帮助。

00:17:25.104 --> 00:17:37.944
Unexplained injuries, fear around a caregiver or unmet basic needs may raise concern. Poverty, illness, difficult housing or a pressure injury alone does not prove abuse.
不明伤、在照顾者旁害怕或基本需求未满足可引担忧；贫困、疾病、住房难或单一压力伤不证明虐待。

00:17:37.944 --> 00:17:47.712
Give the patient a safe chance to speak privately when feasible. Avoid an accusatory confrontation that could increase danger or prevent urgent care.
可行时应让本人有安全私下表达机会；避免指责冲突增加危险或阻碍急救。

00:17:47.712 --> 00:18:00.528
Document location, appearance, observed behavior and the words/source of relevant accounts. Do not date a bruise precisely from color or label a person a perpetrator without evidence.
需记位置外观、所见行为及相关说法原话来源，不能凭颜色精确给瘀伤定龄或无证指人为施害者。

00:18:00.528 --> 00:18:13.536
Respond to immediate danger and use the actual service and British Columbia safeguarding process, with capacity and consent considered. Adult and child reporting rules are not interchangeable.
需应对即时危险，依真实机构及BC保护流程，并考虑能力同意；成人与儿童报告规则不能互换。

00:18:13.536 --> 00:18:22.368
A clear baseline statement can be more useful than simply writing elderly with dementia. Explain the specific new difference.
清楚基线常比只写高龄痴呆有用；应解释具体新差异。

00:18:22.368 --> 00:18:32.760
Attribute collateral and preserve uncertainty about an unwitnessed fall, last medicine dose or onset. Do not fill the record with invented negatives.
旁证要标来源，并保未目击跌、末次药或起始未知，不能编阴性填表。

00:18:32.760 --> 00:18:41.904
Record why a position or movement plan was modified and what happened afterward. Include any incomplete measurement and why it was limited.
应记体位移动为何调整及之后反应，包括未完成测量及局限原因。

00:18:41.904 --> 00:18:51.744
Hand the next team a usable trajectory. A single final normal number does not communicate the patient's actual risk or the preceding deterioration.
要给下队可用过程；最后一个正常值不能沟通真实风险或之前恶化。

00:18:51.744 --> 00:19:00.960
This original patient usually manages ordinary daily tasks and conversation. Today there is a new loss of attention and alertness.
原创患者平时能管日常及交谈，今天新丧注意及清醒程度。

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:11.088
A fall occurred two days earlier, but no reliable witness can confirm head contact. Keep that uncertainty rather than recording no head injury.
两日前跌倒，但无可靠目击可证撞头；需保未知，不能记无头伤。

00:19:11.088 --> 00:19:23.280
The reported medicines change risk: anticoagulation raises bleeding concern and a beta blocker may blunt tachycardia. The exact last doses remain unconfirmed.
转述药史改变风险：抗凝增出血担忧，β阻滞可钝快率；准确末次量仍未核。

00:19:23.280 --> 00:19:34.056
Do not choose between old age, a medicine effect and an injury before assessment. Assess the current threats and obtain a useful timeline in parallel.
评估前不能在年老、药效及伤中先选定一个；需评当前威胁并同步采有用时间线。

00:19:34.056 --> 00:19:44.016
These values are assumed training observations, not real patient data. The normal-range pulse and glucose do not explain away the acute functional change.
这些是训练假设观察，不是真患者数据；范围内脉糖不能抹去急功能变化。

00:19:44.016 --> 00:19:56.496
Assess airway protection and breathing effectiveness, then perfusion and focused neurological findings. The rate of twenty-four and altered response deserve context and reassessment.
应查气道保护及呼吸效能，再看灌注与重点神经；每分24及反应变需背景复评。

00:19:56.496 --> 00:20:07.944
The absence of fever does not exclude infection, and the medicine history prevents relying on pulse alone. The unwitnessed head-contact history also remains relevant.
无热不排感染，药史也使不能只靠脉；未目击撞头史仍相关。

00:20:07.944 --> 00:20:19.056
Do not administer fluid solely because pressure is lower than a reported usual value. Assess the full mechanism and current pathway while arranging appropriate urgent care.
不能只因低于转述平时血压就给液；需评完整机制路径，并安排适当急救。

00:20:19.056 --> 00:20:29.424
Ask for the last confirmed usual conversation and whether function changed immediately after the fall or later. Distinguish observed time from an estimate.
应问末次确认正常交谈，以及跌后立即还是稍后改变，并分实见时间与估计。

00:20:29.424 --> 00:20:42.600
Ask about new pain, vomiting, headache, weakness or speech changes without assuming they must be present. Seek a focused examination rather than forcing painful movement.
要问新痛、吐、头痛、弱或言语变，但不假定必有；应重点查，不强迫疼痛活动。

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:53.208
Clarify last doses and recent changes with permission, using reliable packaging or collateral. Do not infer adherence or overdose from a medicine list.
需经同意用可靠包装旁证澄末次量及近期变，不能从药单推已服或过量。

00:20:53.208 --> 00:21:03.120
Keep infection, metabolic and cardiac alternatives visible. A suspected head injury should not prevent recognition of a second concurrent emergency.
仍需保感染、代谢及心脏替代；疑头伤不能阻止识别第二并发急症。

00:21:03.120 --> 00:21:12.720
Assume a new left-arm weakness is now observed. State precisely what changed rather than inserting a final diagnosis into the case.
假设现观察到新左臂弱，应准确说变化，而非直接塞最终诊断。

00:21:12.720 --> 00:21:25.152
Repeat focused findings and primary threats, and use the applicable stroke or trauma pathway with the full history. The field examination cannot reliably exclude intracranial bleeding.
需复重点发现及主要威胁，带完整史选相应卒中或创伤路径；现场不能可靠排颅内血。

00:21:25.152 --> 00:21:34.680
Preserve the distinct times and uncertainties. The time a deficit is first noticed is not automatically the onset or the last-known-well time.
应分时刻及未知；首次发现缺损不自动是起始或最后正常。

00:21:34.680 --> 00:21:46.416
Pre-alert with the neurological change, anticoagulant history, recent fall and current physiology. Do not delay for an unnecessary walk test or a perfect medication inventory.
应以神经变、抗凝、近期跌及当前生理预警，不为多余试走或完美药清单延误。

00:21:46.416 --> 00:21:56.808
Select a position that supports airway and breathing while respecting the actual injury plan. Avoid forcing kyphotic anatomy into an unsafe flat posture.
需选支持气道呼吸且合真实伤计划的体位，避免强迫后凸解剖危险平放。

00:21:56.808 --> 00:22:05.640
Use the safe movement method justified by current risk and ability. Do not ask the patient to walk simply to save equipment or time.
应依当前风险能力选安全移动，不能只为省器械时间要求走。

00:22:05.640 --> 00:22:15.456
Protect skin and attachments, cover appropriately and keep communication direct. An urgent plan can still preserve privacy and explanation.
需护皮肤附件、适当覆盖并直接沟通；紧急计划仍可保隐私解释。

00:22:15.456 --> 00:22:26.112
Continue checking response during transfer and conveyance. Escalation is not the end of care and a first normal monitor result does not close reassessment.
转移途中仍需查反应，升级不是照护终点，首次监测正常也不能结束复评。

00:22:26.112 --> 00:22:34.896
Begin with the meaningful change from baseline and the current concern. Give relevant times and the reliability of each source.
应先报相对基线的重要变化及当前担忧，再给相关时间及各来源可靠性。

00:22:34.896 --> 00:22:44.424
Report medicines and injury facts without overstating certainty. Use unknown rather than a fabricated no when information is absent.
药伤事实不能过度确定；无资料时应说未知，而不是编一个无。

00:22:44.424 --> 00:22:54.648
Describe the actual neurological and physiological trend and the response to care. A label such as elderly fall or possible UTI is not enough.
要描述真实神经生理趋势及照护反应，只称高龄跌倒或可能UTI不够。

00:22:54.648 --> 00:23:05.904
Explain movement modifications and remaining threats. The receiving team needs a reliable clinical story, not a collection of reassuring isolated numbers.
需解释移动调整及剩余威胁，接收队要可靠故事，不是一堆看似放心的孤立数值。

00:23:05.904 --> 00:23:16.560
You should be able to recognize new illness even when pain, fever or tachycardia is absent. That requires a real baseline and a complete primary assessment.
应能在无痛、热或快率时认新病，这需真实基线及完整主要评估。

00:23:16.560 --> 00:23:25.032
Explain how medicines and reserve alter the presentation without making the drug list or the patient's age the final diagnosis.
需解释药物储备如何改表现，但不把药单或年龄当最终诊断。

00:23:25.032 --> 00:23:34.584
Demonstrate supported communication and safe movement using the actual tools and authorization. Preserve dignity as part of clinical quality.
需用真实工具授权演支持沟通及安全移动，把尊严当临床质量一部分。

00:23:34.584 --> 00:23:43.848
Then reassess and report the trajectory. The same baseline-change-modification framework will guide the next session on larger-bodied patients.
之后要复评并报过程，同一基线、变化、调整框架将用于下节大体型患者。
